        "input": "\n"
      }
    }
  ]
}

Confirming this. I just chased the same bug — running `openai/gpt-5.5` via Codex OAuth on a Pro/Plus plan, compaction kicks in around ~250k tokens despite the model having 922k input / 1M context.

Root cause is exactly what you identified: `CodexAuthPlugin.auth.loader` in `packages/opencode/src/plugin/codex.ts:394-402` unconditionally replaces `model.limit` for any `gpt-5.5` model:

```ts
if (model.id.includes("gpt-5.5")) {
  model.limit = {
    context: 400_000,
    input: 272_000,
    output: 128_000,
  }
}
```

The user-config override in `provider.ts` runs *after* this, but only applies fields the user explicitly set:

```ts
if (configLimit) {
  if (configLimit.context) model.limit.context = configLimit.context
  if (configLimit.input) model.limit.input = configLimit.input
  if (configLimit.output) model.limit.output = configLimit.output
}
```

So a user who only sets `{ context: 1050000, output: 128000 }` (the natural pattern, since `input` is implied) silently keeps `input: 272000` from the plugin hardcode. With `usable() = input - reserved = 252_000`, compaction triggers at the first 250k+ message.

**Debug evidence** — the relevant overflow check from a real session before the workaround:

```
service=session.overflow modelID=gpt-5.5 
  tokens={"total":647998,"input":1,"output":158,"reasoning":0,"cache":{"write":524,"read":647315}} 
  count=647998 limit=252000 overflow=true 
  modelLimit={"context":1050000,"input":272000,"output":128000}
```

Note `modelLimit.input=272000` despite `context=1050000` — that's the user's `context` override applied while `input` stayed at the codex hardcode.

**Workaround**: explicitly add all three fields to user config:

```jsonc
"openai": {
  "models": {
    "gpt-5.5": {
      "limit": {
        "context": 1050000,
        "input": 922000,   // <-- this is the field that gets silently overwritten
        "output": 128000
      }
    }
  }
}
```

**Proposed real fix**: when user provides any explicit `limit` override, fall back to the original models.dev snapshot for unspecified fields (not to whatever a plugin auth.loader has mutated the limit to). I have an implementation on a fork: https://github.com/sjawhar/opencode/commit/f4ab23a6270e — it captures the original limits before plugin loaders run, then uses them as the fallback in the override loop. The plugin still gets to enforce its restriction when no user override exists, but the user's intent wins when they have explicitly configured the model.

Tested with the same gpt-5.5 + Codex OAuth setup — compaction now correctly fires near the 902k threshold (922k input - 20k reserved) instead of 252k.
